    "body": "I've confirmed this bug and I believe we don't have any web platform test coverage for it.\n\n@noamr would you be willing to help fix this?\n\nI'm not sure where the best place to insert the popstate firing step is. [Blink's implementation](https://source.chromium.org/chromium/chromium/src/+/main:third_party/blink/renderer/core/loader/document_loader.cc;l=1178-1193;drc=5f81609f7c343a17175b71d07ae02d6f5d09675f) puts it at the bottom of the URL and history update steps, with a boolean parameter controlling when to do so which is set in complicated ways by the callers. But Blink's implementation of and call sites of the URL and history change steps is pretty different from the spec's.\n\nWe could just put it in \"navigate to a fragment\", but that will no longer be a suitable location after we introduce deferred commit (#10919).\n\nWe could put it in \"inner navigate event firing algorithm\", after \"URL and history update steps\" in the push/replace case. But we'd need to thread through some extra state to distinguish the fragment navigation case (should fire) from all other cases (should not fire). I guess this is pretty similar to Blink's strategy in some ways. [This recent Chromium change](https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/c/chromium/src/+/6299859) would be helpful if we go this route.",
